  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You become wholly suffused with the wild's ancient and terrible power, granting you the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Ominous Strikes.</strong> When you hit a creature that has the Frightened condition with an attack roll, the attack deals extra damage equal to your Wisdom modifier.</p><p><strong>Persistent Wrath.</strong> If you are reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright while transformed by Wrath of the Wild, you can surge with wild power: your Hit Points instead change to twice your Ranger level. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest, but you can expend a level 4+ spell slot (no action required) to restore its use.</p><p><strong>Timeless.</strong> You have Immunity to the Exhaustion condition.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-aJWBP5AVA4MhgA8h\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Ominous Strikes deals the damage type of your attack. Restoring Persistent Wrath needs a level 4+ slot.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
